This game was a lot of fun. I got ticked off with my valkyries early in 
the tournament and just couldn't ascend one, but managed on my first try 
with a wizard.

I had a very lucky start; my pet and I managed to get to gnometown while 
I was still level 1. I sold a bunch of my gear and things I found in the 
shop to raise 800 zorkmids to pay for protection. The altar turned out 
to be coaligned, and I managed to sacrifice some monsters to Thoth. I 
camped the altar until I got magicbane around lvl 5. It helped that my 
wizard was generated with a spellbook of create monster.

To top that off, there was a magic lamp in one of the stores. I blessed 
it and wished for a suit of silver dragon scale mail.

My large cat had a worse time of it and lost a fight to a guard. RIP fluffy.

Back to the main dungeon. I had a nice AC but I kept losing my 
protection. Still, AC of -9 was nice to have. I found an amulet of 
reflection in Sokoban (darnit) and got the luckstone from the bottom of 
the mines. I still didn't have any containers, so I had to make stashes 
periodically.

I took things very slow; I probably didn't even reach the castle until 
around turn 20,000. I altar camped a lot, got some good spellbooks, 
managed to get crowned, and built up my skills in divination, attack and 
matter spells. I found a spellbook of polymorph and managed to poly 
about 257 items during the course of the game.

The castle was a pain. I nearly got killed a few times by minotaurs and 
liches summoning monsters. I managed to get to the up stairs to heal up, 
but the only thing that really saved me was my charm monster spell. I 
charmed a titan, a xorn, and a bunch of other monsters and waged war. 
Eventually I managed to get the wand of wishing and wished for a bag of 
holding, a helm of brilliance, some magic markers and speed boots along 
with the requisite charging scrolls (although in retrospect if I'd been 
smart I would have just wished for the markers and then wrote the 
scrolls). I fixed up my armor and returned to the main dungeon.

I went on the quest and had no real problems. Being expert in attack 
spells, I did away with any mind flayer types quickly and ruthlessly. 
Liches I simply pummeled with magicbane.

Along the way I managed to locate Ft. Ludios and loot it. The soldiers 
never stood a chance and it was fun using finger of death against them.

I did manage to poly some unicorn horns into a magic marker. That was 
fairly useful, but if I had to do it all over again I would have made 
sure to write some detect treasure scrolls to get through the endgame 
easier. Bumbling through that nearly cost me.

I kept polying rings hoping for a ring of levitation but one never 
materialized. I polyed a lot of glass into gems.

I explored Gehennom, and for the first time I didn't use a pickaxe. I 
used dig spells when I wanted to make a gap in the walls, or a wand of 
digging when I was low on power. I had plenty of wands. It certainly 
helped with encumberance and I was rarely burdened.

I went back to the main dungeon and did some nurse dancing, and reverse 
geno'd wraiths. Around turn 35,000 I figured I was ready.

I used cone of cold to cross water and FoD'd Rodney. Unfortunately, 
somewhere along the way I decided in my infinite wisdom that I should 
get rid of my amulet of ESP and don one of the 5 amulets of life saving 
I had found. This caused me to step into a doorway where a master mind 
flayer was waiting. My ascension run just got more interesting due to 
the fact that I had forgotten the maps for several levels.

Still, I managed to get back to the vibrating square and perform the 
ritual. The high priest was a pushover. The worst part was Rodney and 
liches summoning nasties.

I had a nice walk back to the main dungeon, covering one of the levels 4 
times. Once I got out of Gehennom it was a nice restful journey until 
the plane of earth.

I killed Rodney yet again, fished into my pack for some scrolls of 
detect treasure, and discovered that they had been blanked by a dip into 
a moat while confused. I had to manually navigate each plane.

Earth wasn't bad - I ran right into the portal fairly fast.

Air wasn't too bad either - I had conflict, and only had to drink 1 
potion of full healing. I did have to waste several charges of my wands 
of death, however.

Fire was pretty scary. Several archons summons hordes and hordes of 
nasties, and I was surrounded by a 5x5 grid of monsters. To make it even 
more interesting, I was constantly removing blindness and stunning effects.

Just when I thought I had gotten away, a rock troll put on a pair of 
leather gloves, picked up a c corpse, and stoned me. Goodbye AoLS #1.

I quickly put on my 2nd amulet. The rock troll hit me again, and I 
started slowing down. I FoD'd him, and burned the 2nd amulet. I then 
took off my boots of levitation, confiscated the c corpse while the 
troll was still out, and began stoning monsters - including the stupid 
archons who caused most of the trouble to begin with. I eventually found 
the portal and left.

On water I discovered that a master mind flayer had caused me to forget 
which ring was my ring of slow digestion. Unfortunately, it turned out 
that it was gone. I suspect Rodney stole it during one of his visits. I 
was getting hungry and didn't plan for that.

Luckily, some giants and a few dragons happened along on Rodney's next 
visit. I ate the corpses and got satiated status, then found the last 
portal.

I headed for the middle altar because death was guarding it. I managed 
to get around death and some angels, head to the altar (which was the 
correct one) and sacrified the amulet. Woo hoo!

So despite plenty of mistakes, there was no lasting harm done.

